WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:04.560
(gentle music)

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.920
- Hey, guys, it's me, Jasmine

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.287
and I forgot.

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:09.150
(Katy laughs)

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.550
Hey, everyone, it's me, Jasmine

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.720
and Lunar New Year is
right around the corner.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.300
If you know anything about Lunar New Year,

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.810
the most important thing, the food.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.790
Today, I'll be showing
you three sweet treats

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.769
that I grew up eating while
celebrating Lunar New Year

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:22.700
on my Taiwanese family's side.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.180
There's a whole list of different food,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.270
both sweet and savory,

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.570
to be eaten during Lunar
New Year festivities

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.640
and these are just three out of many

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.894
that I loved from my childhood.

00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:32.840
Many different cultures
celebrate Lunar New Year

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.350
in their own way

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.710
and they all have their
own special traditions,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.510
although many also overlap.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.055
So Lunar New Year
celebrates the first year

00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:42.446
of the lunar-solar calendar.

00:00:42.446 --> 00:00:44.191
You might have heard Lunar New Year

00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:45.070
being called Chinese New Year.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.010
That really encompasses
Chinese New Year traditions.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.740
Lunar New Year encompasses all
different kinds of cultures

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.830
that celebrate this calendar date,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.570
so you might see Koreans
say Happy Korean New Year.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.980
Vietnamese people celebrate Tet

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.500
or say Happy Vietnamese New Year.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.630
Every culture has their
own special traditions.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.010
The first treat we're making
are fried sesame balls.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.780
They're deliciously crispy yet chewy

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.295
and have a beautiful nuttiness

00:01:07.295 --> 00:01:09.510
from both the sesame
seeds and the red beans.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.930
They are super popular to
eat during Lunar New Year.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.930
The round shape and golden
colors stand for good luck

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.470
and they also increasingly
grow in size while cooking

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.610
which stands for growing prosperity.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.560
So to begin, we have some red beans

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.350
that have been soaking overnight.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.080
This is what they look
like before soaking.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.984
We wanna soak them to one,
reduce the cooking time

00:01:29.984 --> 00:01:31.760
and two, make them more digestible.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.070
We're gonna start by draining these.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.170
We're gonna add water to a pot

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.880
and then add in our beans.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.910
So once this is boiling,

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.810
we're gonna cover it up and
let it cook for an hour.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.901
You'll see that they
are soft, they're plump.

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.797
Most of the water has cooked down

00:01:45.797 --> 00:01:46.980
so we are now gonna add some sugar

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.160
and we're just gonna mix
this until it thickens

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.640
into a paste.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.455
Get your aggression out.

00:01:52.455 --> 00:01:54.047
Think of every aunty that has asked you,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.967
"When are you gonna get married?

00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:57.727
"Do you have a partner?

00:01:57.727 --> 00:01:59.380
"How much money do you make?"

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.213
I'm in love!

00:02:01.418 --> 00:02:02.251
Just kidding, everything is fine.

00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:04.640
Let's transfer this to our bowl

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.630
and as it cools, you'll notice

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.760
that it starts to slightly thicken.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.767
Our red bean paste is ready.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:10.600
Let's get to making the dough.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.733
First, I have some brown sugar here

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:13.566
and some hot water.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.890
I'm gonna pour it over my brown sugar

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.362
and we're just gonna mix it all up

00:02:17.362 --> 00:02:18.983
until it fully dissolves.

00:02:18.983 --> 00:02:20.800
So I have some glutinous
rice flour over here.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.390
The glutinous rice flour is so important.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.460
It gives it that mochi texture.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.709
So don't use all-purpose flour.

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:28.542
You're gonna be so sad.

00:02:28.542 --> 00:02:30.265
Okay, so with the flour,

00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:32.381
I'm going to create a well in the center

00:02:32.381 --> 00:02:34.340
and then we're gonna pour
in our brown sugar syrup

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.650
and now we're just gonna stir
this for about five minutes

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.740
until everything's fully
combined and the dough is smooth.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.480
I know it looks a little wet right now

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.581
but we're gonna start kneading it

00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:45.364
and it will firm up.

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.810
So let's transfer our dough to my floured

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.390
and clean counter.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.530
So I like to flour my hands first

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.920
to keep it from getting sticky.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.110
Start incorporating everything together

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.860
and we're just gonna knead
this for about five minutes.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.360
Perfect, so our dough looks about ready.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.090
You can see that it's
much firmer than before.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.703
Time to assemble.

00:03:05.703 --> 00:03:08.420
So first, we're going
to cut our dough in half

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.550
and we're gonna roll these out into logs

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.440
until I have eight pieces of dough.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.797
So with each of our
divided pieces of dough,

00:03:16.797 --> 00:03:18.162
we're gonna roll them into balls.

00:03:18.162 --> 00:03:19.634
And every time you have a finished ball,

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.258
go ahead and place a
damp paper towel over it

00:03:22.258 --> 00:03:23.474
to keep it from drying.

00:03:23.474 --> 00:03:24.310
I'm gonna finish rolling out these balls

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.810
and then we'll get to filling them.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.020
So it's time to assemble.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.670
We're just gonna work with one at a time.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.120
Remember to keep your damp towel over

00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:34.290
the rest of your dough babies.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.481
I saw a comment the other day.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.487
It was like, "Why do all Tasty producers

00:03:36.487 --> 00:03:38.640
"call their doughs dough babies?"

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.810
- [Katy] Why do we do that?
- I know.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.813
I have no clue why.

00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:42.646
Flatten it.

00:03:42.646 --> 00:03:45.210
So now I am going to pinch the sides

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.802
so that it's slightly thinner
than the rest of the dough.

00:03:48.802 --> 00:03:50.180
Totally fine if you get
some cracks like this.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.066
It'll still work.

00:03:52.066 --> 00:03:54.120
We're gonna take one
teaspoon of red bean paste.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.620
I usually just scoop it out
with my finger like this.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.550
And we're just gonna seal it.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:03:59.597
Once it's sealed,

00:03:59.597 --> 00:04:01.130
you can put this face down on the counter

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.480
and just give it a slow swirl

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.380
and it'll close up on itself.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.301
And now we're coat it in our sesame seeds.

00:04:08.301 --> 00:04:09.134
Make sure it's evenly coated.

00:04:09.134 --> 00:04:11.646
You can sprinkle them on like this

00:04:11.646 --> 00:04:13.530
or you can just go ahead
and carefully push it around

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.380
until it's fully covered
in the sesame seeds.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.010
I'm gonna make seven more of these,

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.110
fishing off the dough,

00:04:19.946 --> 00:04:21.760
and then we will get to cooking them.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.460
I have some vegetable oil in
a pot and I brought it to 350

00:04:25.496 --> 00:04:28.013
and I'm just gonna fry
about four of them at once

00:04:28.013 --> 00:04:28.846
for 15 minutes.

00:04:28.846 --> 00:04:31.020
Once it puffs up, it
kinda lives on one side

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.214
so you're gonna wanna kind of flip it

00:04:33.214 --> 00:04:35.096
so that it's evenly
cooked and golden brown.

00:04:35.096 --> 00:04:36.010
Typically we eat these on Lunar New Year

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.460
because the round shape
and the golden color

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.050
symbolizes good luck.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.980
Also, you'll see as we
fry these, they'll puff up

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:47.362
and they'll increasingly
swell while we're frying it

00:04:47.362 --> 00:04:48.880
which stands for growing prosperity.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.210
When they start to float to the top,

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.630
I know it's almost done and
the magic is about to happen

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.160
oh my gosh, look at that.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.750
It is so pretty.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.590
Beautifully round, golden brown,

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.810
and look how big it got.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.360
This is the original size.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.216
Now that these guys are done,

00:05:04.216 --> 00:05:05.350
we're gonna transfer them to a wire rack.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.450
These are done frying.

00:05:07.284 --> 00:05:08.376
We're gonna fry up the rest of them

00:05:08.376 --> 00:05:10.530
and then do a little taste test. Yay!

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.720
All of our fried sesame balls
are done. They are so pretty.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.740
Look at that golden brown sheen.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.050
The sesame seeds are nice and toasty.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.773
I can't wait to dig in.
Let's give it a try.

00:05:18.773 --> 00:05:19.606
Cheers!

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.653
Oh my gosh.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:23.733
Look at that.

00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:26.063
Nicely sweet, red bean filling.

00:05:27.204 --> 00:05:28.570
The mochi in between the outside,

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.480
so, so chewy,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.500
and the outside has that fried flavor,

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.970
but not too oily, so good.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.140
Let's move on to the next one.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.820
My mom's favorite.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.090
The second treat we'll be baking up

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.095
are these fortune cakes,

00:05:41.095 --> 00:05:43.680
also referred to as prosperity
cakes or lucky cakes

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.897
and are extremely popular
during Lunar New Year.

00:05:46.897 --> 00:05:47.980
The name (speaks foreign
language) sounds like wealth,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.340
thus symbolizing good
fortune for the new year.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.680
So to our small sauce pan,

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.173
we're gonna add our brown
sugar, butter, and water.

00:05:56.241 --> 00:05:57.563
So we're just gonna stir this

00:05:57.563 --> 00:05:58.910
until the sugar dissolves,
about five minutes.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.840
Now that everything is
dissolved and has come together,

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.620
we are going to remove this from heat

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.300
and let is cool to room temperature.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.133
Let's make the batter.

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.720
First, we're gonna add
our self-rising flour.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.120
Sift that in there.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.220
Also, our rice flour.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.350
Not glutinous, regular rice flour.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.330
And then our baking powder.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.993
Now we're gonna quickly
whisk this together

00:06:18.993 --> 00:06:19.900
so that it's combined.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.800
Bring back our syrup here.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.170
Now we're gonna fold it in.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.230
You really just wanna mix this

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.870
until you don't have any flour clumps

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.443
because that is not fun to eat.

00:06:28.358 --> 00:06:30.380
So the molds we're using
today are egg tart molds.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.091
If you don't have them
at home, don't worry.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.905
You can totally use cupcake liners.

00:06:33.905 --> 00:06:36.507
We're gonna take some
batter and fill it in there,

00:06:36.507 --> 00:06:37.809
all the way to the top.

00:06:37.809 --> 00:06:39.120
These cakes, they're deceiving.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.430
It's got flavor, but it's light.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:42.580
It's so delicious

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.699
and you can't really eat one.

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:45.920
It's super addicting and the texture of it

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.970
is very different than a muffin.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.270
These are usually on the table

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.980
once you show up to a
Lunar New Year festivity.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.840
Some people eat it as they get in

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.130
for a little snack before the meal.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.760
Some people eat it for dessert.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.070
My personal favorite

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.640
is to save it for the next morning

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.950
and have it for breakfast.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.120
So I was a little generous
with my previous molds

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.721
and I've run out of
batter for the last one

00:07:08.721 --> 00:07:10.270
so I'm just gonna top this one off

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:14.438
with the remaining and let's get steaming.

00:07:14.438 --> 00:07:16.900
Okay, our steamer basket
is rapidly boiling

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.940
so we're gonna steam these in batches.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:22.360
My steamer basket will allow
for about three at one time

00:07:23.546 --> 00:07:24.379
and they do expand a little bit,

00:07:24.379 --> 00:07:27.310
so try to space them out if you can.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.440
We're gonna cover this up

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.540
and steam for about 20 minutes.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.570
Do not, do not open the lid.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.430
Bad fortune for the year if you open it.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.140
- [Katy] Is that true
or did you make that up?

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:37.300
- I made that up.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.300
Our fortune cakes are done

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.983
and they've cracked on top,

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:42.910
which is exactly what we want.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.350
A little background behind this.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.270
Growing up, people
would say it's good luck

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.790
because it's a smile and
that brings happiness

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:53.115
to your new year, but I
remember seeing this as a kid

00:07:53.115 --> 00:07:54.860
and thinking, that is a scary smile.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.390
And then I was told another story

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.230
which is that this is like a flower

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.720
and each time it cracks,
it makes a new petal.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.730
The more petals you get,

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.560
the more luck you have in the new year.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.900
So these ones, this is
probably the one I would go for

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.733
as a kid.

00:08:06.733 --> 00:08:07.566
Cheers.

00:08:08.975 --> 00:08:09.998
(light music)

00:08:09.998 --> 00:08:11.240
Mmm.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.230
Oh my gosh.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:15.450
The texture is light yet chewy and dense.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.460
It's sweet, it's savory.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.890
I love that this is perfect
for any time of the day.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.830
Breakfast, lunch, dinner, snack, dessert.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.680
All right, this was really good,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.200
but let's move on to the next
one which is my favorite.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.090
These last ones, probably
my favorites for the day.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.590
Glutinous rice balls or
(speaks foreign language).

00:08:33.808 --> 00:08:35.210
They symbolize reunion and togetherness

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.230
and are considered a good-luck food

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.640
to bring at a peaceful and happy new year.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.520
They sit in a light yet flavorful

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.430
brown sugar ginger syrup
that is so scrumptious

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.660
and so refreshing.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.803
We'll start by making the filling.

00:08:47.803 --> 00:08:48.920
So this one is my favorite.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.899
This is the black sesame for
the black sesame filling.

00:08:51.899 --> 00:08:53.819
We are gonna start my toasting this.

00:08:53.819 --> 00:08:55.333
It's a little hard to see

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:56.739
once they're nicely toasted

00:08:56.739 --> 00:08:58.270
because the color doesn't really change.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.155
You'll know when it's done

00:09:00.155 --> 00:09:01.859
when you get that nutty aroma.

00:09:01.859 --> 00:09:02.820
Now that it's beautifully toasted,

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:06.220
we are going to transfer
this to our food processor.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.413
Toss in our sugar,

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:11.803
and we're gonna process--
(processor whirs)

00:09:11.803 --> 00:09:14.811
(Jasmine laughs)

00:09:14.811 --> 00:09:17.752
So now we're gonna process
this until it becomes a paste.

00:09:17.752 --> 00:09:19.730
(processor whirs)

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.780
Perfect, now we're
gonna add in some butter

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.170
and then we're gonna process it again

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:26.191
until it becomes the consistency
of like a nut butter.

00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:28.516
(food processor whirs)

00:09:28.516 --> 00:09:29.966
All my black sesame desserts.

00:09:30.818 --> 00:09:33.143
I love this in a bun. This
in a milk tea, oh my God.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.449
All right, let's transfer this to a bowl

00:09:35.449 --> 00:09:36.316
and then we're gonna repeat

00:09:36.316 --> 00:09:37.149
the same with our peanut filling.

00:09:37.149 --> 00:09:40.874
So same steps as last
time, except with peanuts.

00:09:40.874 --> 00:09:43.360
Great, these peanuts look like
they are beautifully toasted.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.423
Let's process this in the food processor.

00:09:46.868 --> 00:09:47.790
Our sugar.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.724
And we're gonna process this.

00:09:49.724 --> 00:09:51.320
(processor whirs)

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.200
Perfect.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.974
We're gonna toss in our butter.

00:09:53.974 --> 00:09:56.350
(food processor whirs)

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.400
Look at this.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.720
Look at the consistency of this.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.399
This looks great.

00:10:01.399 --> 00:10:02.232
We're gonna put both the peanut

00:10:02.232 --> 00:10:03.670
and black sesame fillings in the fridge

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.716
to chill for an hour.

00:10:04.716 --> 00:10:06.552
I'll be right back. Our fillings
are now out of the fridge.

00:10:06.552 --> 00:10:07.550
Look how firm they are.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.080
So this will make 10 fillings.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.280
I'm gonna break it in half

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:13.540
and we're gonna do five
from each of these.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.563
So we're just gonna roll it into balls.

00:10:16.402 --> 00:10:17.388
There's always a debate.

00:10:17.388 --> 00:10:18.410
Do you like your glutinous rice balls

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.220
in a hot broth or a cold broth?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.140
And my answer is always cold.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.723
I feel like it's so refreshing.

00:10:25.649 --> 00:10:28.143
We're gonna repeat this
with our peanut filling,

00:10:28.143 --> 00:10:30.110
pre-portioning them out again.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:31.550
Okay, wonderful.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:35.280
Anything that is food
in ball form is so cute.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.340
Okay, let's make the
brown sugar ginger syrup.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.120
So in a pot over medium heat,

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.003
I'm going to add some hot water,

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.003
brown sugar.

00:10:43.992 --> 00:10:46.100
If you like it sweeter, feel
free to add more brown sugar.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.260
I'm just thinking about
my mom watching this video

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.360
being like, why'd you add so much sugar?

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.510
And of course, some ginger.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:55.672
Now we're gonna stir it
until the sugar is dissolved

00:10:55.672 --> 00:10:58.623
and let that cook for about
three to five minutes.

00:10:59.489 --> 00:11:00.322
The sugar's fully dissolved.

00:11:00.322 --> 00:11:02.410
I am going to let this
cool to room temperature

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.120
and then I'm gonna throw
it in the fridge to cool.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.170
Let's make the dough.

00:11:06.339 --> 00:11:07.670
So we're starting with
some glutinous rice flour.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.180
Quarter cup of boiling water.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.510
All right, just gonna
give this a quick whisk.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:15.250
Now I'm gonna add in a quarter cup

00:11:16.106 --> 00:11:18.094
of room temperature water.

00:11:18.094 --> 00:11:20.526
I'm gonna switch over to my spatula here.

00:11:20.526 --> 00:11:22.414
Okay, this looks roughly combined.

00:11:22.414 --> 00:11:25.550
Let's transfer this to our counter

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:27.880
and we are just gonna
continue to knead this

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.847
for about two to three minutes

00:11:29.847 --> 00:11:32.240
just until the dough is nice and smooth.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.245
I didn't make glutinous
rice balls growing up.

00:11:35.245 --> 00:11:36.340
My family would go and get it

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.110
as sort of a special occasion,

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.667
but I think I made it a
little more special (laughs).

00:11:41.824 --> 00:11:43.130
Like it was like a little
treat once in a while.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.990
I like to roll it into a little log,

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.280
divide it into two.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.910
This one will stay here and
it's gonna remain white.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.810
I'm gonna put this one
in my bowl from earlier

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:55.100
and I'm gonna add a couple
drops of pink food coloring.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.820
While you're not working
on the white dough here,

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.060
make sure o cover it
with a damp paper towel

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.710
so it doesn't dry out.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:03.900
So, to mix this, if you like
to get your hands dirty,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.650
by all means, but I'm gonna put on a glove

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:09.030
so it doesn't look so gruesome.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.210
These are nice gloves.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.570
So I actually like to coat it like this.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:13.720
Like a dumpling.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.710
So it stays inside.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.920
And then I'll just continue
folding it over and over.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.500
Once it's pretty generally dispersed,

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.430
then you can knead it on the counter.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:25.650
If you don't wanna use food coloring,

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.290
you can use beet juice.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:28.173
It looks so good.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.943
Feel like playing Super Smash now.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.860
So now we have both our doughs here.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.420
So with each piece of dough,

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.690
I am going to divide it into 10 pieces.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.283
About a tablespoon per piece.

00:12:41.478 --> 00:12:42.827
(upbeat music)

00:12:42.827 --> 00:12:44.050
So now we're gonna roll these into balls

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:47.430
and when you're done, just
place them on a tray next to you

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.020
and then I'm gonna continue doing this

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.890
until I have all my dough rolled out

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:52.500
and then we'll get to filling them.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.200
Look at all these beautiful balls.

00:12:55.307 --> 00:12:56.480
(Katy laughs)

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.313
Katy!

00:12:58.187 --> 00:12:59.190
- [Katy] Sorry.

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.053
- (laughs) This is a family holiday.

00:13:02.752 --> 00:13:03.585
So what you're gonna do,

00:13:03.585 --> 00:13:05.310
I like to just press
it down in the center.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.460
So we're gonna put this
on top of your hand,

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.400
press it down to the center,

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:13.457
and place a filling inside,

00:13:13.457 --> 00:13:15.780
and then I start to
loosen up on the bottom

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:18.110
and start working my fingers upwards.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.150
Press it down

00:13:20.694 --> 00:13:23.310
until you can get it fully enclosed.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:27.000
Once it's sealed, you can
roll it again on the counter

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.530
or on your palms.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.950
You can see it's cracking on the outside.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:30.783
That's fine.

00:13:31.659 --> 00:13:34.173
So let's place this back here.
Same thing with the peanut.

00:13:34.173 --> 00:13:36.390
With our white dough,
we're gonna press flat.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.190
Make sure to not make the dough too thin

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.488
or else it could crack

00:13:40.488 --> 00:13:42.150
and all the filling would burst

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:45.640
and be released into your boiling water.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.810
So I put the peanut filling inside.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:48.870
Same thing.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:51.520
We're just gonna wrap
it and seal it closed.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.710
All right, I am gonna finish
assembling the rest of these.

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.370
Usually, the whole family is helping

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:58.060
but I'm on my own today.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.700
I have some water in a pot here

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.730
and we are going to boil six at a time.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.880
I'm totally okay to combine both of them.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.453
So drop it in gently.

00:14:08.607 --> 00:14:09.440
It'll stick to the bottom of your pan,

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:12.090
so you just wanna carefully stir it.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.510
They're finally floating

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.331
and we've cooked them for another minute.

00:14:16.331 --> 00:14:17.696
They are looking absolutely good

00:14:17.696 --> 00:14:19.530
and we are going to put
them in the ice bath,

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.390
but before we do that,
we have to check them

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.330
to see if any of them burst

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:25.360
because if they do, they
do not go in the ice bath

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.620
because that ice bath
will just go directly

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.170
inside the rice bowl.

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:30.683
Luckily, they all look great.

00:14:31.538 --> 00:14:33.680
Just a quick ice bath,
place them in your bowl.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.660
Now I'm gonna pour the syrup

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.070
over my slotted spoon
so none of that ginger

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.910
goes into my dessert.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:41.782
So here we have it.

00:14:41.782 --> 00:14:42.615
The glutinous rice balls

00:14:42.615 --> 00:14:43.870
otherwise known as
(speaks foreign language).

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.260
My favorite.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.761
I'm super excited to dig in.

00:14:47.761 --> 00:14:48.763
Let's give it a try.

00:14:48.763 --> 00:14:50.129
Make sure you get some broth.

00:14:50.129 --> 00:14:51.687
Cheers.

00:14:51.687 --> 00:14:52.520
(upbeat music)

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:53.910
Mmm.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.484
Black sesame,

00:14:55.484 --> 00:14:57.990
the flavor is just this rich nuttiness

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:00.810
that doesn't compare to
other nuts and seeds.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.030
It's so special.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:03.460
All right, y'all, that was so good.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.150
I hope you had a good time

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.980
making these Lunar New
Year treats with me.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.520
If you make any of these recipes

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:11.100
or celebrate Lunar New Year
in your own special way,

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.270
make sure to snap a picture
and tag me on Instagram.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.750
Happy New Year!

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.090
Or as we say at home
(speaks foreign language).

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:17.923
Bye!

00:15:18.842 --> 00:15:21.592
(cheerful music)

